[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=1]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (0,3.9);
\coordinate (C) at (-3.1,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,right] {$r$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,above left] {$t$};
\draw (C)--(A) node[midway,below] {$s$};
\coordinate (ra1) at ($(A)!0.32cm!(B)$);
\coordinate (ra2) at ($(A)!0.32cm!(C)$);
\draw (ra1)--($(ra1)+(ra2)-(A)$)--(ra2);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.62cm,angle eccentricity=1.75] {angle=A--C--B};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
For the marked angle $\theta$, which name belongs to side $r$?

